{
    "background_story": "Zaid was a philosopher-king who ruled his kingdom with a singular focus on the greater good. He believed in the principles of utilitarianism, where the right action was the one that maximized overall happiness and well-being. Zaid made it his mission to improve the lives of his subjects, investing in infrastructure, education, and healthcare. He implemented policies that promoted fairness, justice, and equality, often putting the needs of the many above the interests of the few. When a severe drought hit the land, Zaid made the difficult decision to redistribute the kingdom's resources, ensuring that everyone had access to food and water, even if it meant sacrificing some of his own privileges. His selfless leadership earned him the respect and admiration of his people, who thrived under his utilitarian rule.",
